silon=0.05,\n74-        )\n75-        contours = ComputeIsocontours(\n--\n233-\n234-DATA LOADERS (ROOT NODES)\n235--------------------------\n236-\n237:Note: Assume that all fields loaded are piecewise linear and defined on regular grids. A \n238-      triangulation or tetrahedralization is implicitly assumed.\n239-\n240-LoadScalarField(load_path, arrayName=\"\")\n241-    Loads a scalar field. load_path is a VTI or time-series directory. arrayName is\n--\n279-\n280-SCALAR OPERATIONS AND TOPOLOGICAL STRUCTURES\n281---------------------------------------------\n282-\n283:PersistenceSimplification(parent_node_id, epsilon, threshold_is_absolute)\n284-    Simplifies a scalar field. epsilon is a fraction of the function range: 0 means\n285-    no simplification and 1 spans the entire range. Set threshold_is_absolute to True\n286-    to specify that epsilon is an absolute threshold and False for relative.\n287-\n288:ComputePersistenceDiagram(parent_node_id)\n289:    Computes a scalar field's piecewise linear persistence diagram using the FTM backend.\n290-\n291:EmbedPersistenceDiagram(parent_node_id, ball_radius=0.02, tube_radius=0.01)\n292-    Displays persistence pairs as balls and tubes. Both radii are fractions of the\n293-    scalar function range.\n294-\n295-ComputeMorseSmaleSegmentation(parent_node_id)\n296:    Computes the piecewise linear Morse-Smale segmentation of a scalar field.\n297-\n298-EmbedMorseSmaleSegmentation(parent_node_id)\n299-    Creates displayable geometry for a Morse-Smale segmentation.\n300-\n--\n305-    Displays isocontours with the selected colormap. tube_radius is the contour tube\n306-    radius used for 2D data.\n307-\n308-ComputeContourTree(parent_node_id)\n309:    Computes a scalar field's piecewise linear contour tree.\n310-\n311-EmbedContourTree(parent_node_id, ball_radius=3.0, tube_radius=1.5,\n312-                 color_scheme=[\"#002fff\", \"#758fff\", \"#ffdee7\", \"#ff0046\",\n313-                               \"#000000\"])\n--\n3